    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "— aIr nEw ZEaLanD\nFor your Safety-Please Read\nPlease do not remove this folder from the aircraft\nExperienced passengers review the safety instructions\nbefore take-off and landing\nFor your safety, know how to move out of this airplane - fast.\n(There is fire danger anytime a landing is other than normal)\nFamiliarise yourself with your exit locations.\nKnow how to jump into the escape slide.\nKnow how to put on your lifejacket quickly.\nKnow where the nearest liferaft is positioned.\nB747\nINTERNATIONEE\nFasten\nFold up\nTray\nStow\nluggage\nunder\nseat\nUnfasten\nTake-off/Landing\nNo Smoking\nFor safety, keep seat\nbelts comfortably\nfastened at all times\nSeat Belts\nBrace Position\nDon't use in flight",
      "Adult / Child Lifejacket\nInfant's Jacket\nWater Landing\nTop Deck\nMove away from\nslide areas\nJUMP -\nDON'T SIT)\nExits and Escape Slides\nRemember\nThere are 11 exits.\nKnow where your exits are.\nFind the exits for your section.\nIn the event of an evacuation,\nmove quickly to the exit\nand jump onto the escape slide.\nAlways remove your shoes.\nDon't take any hand luggage\nwith you.\nPointsto Remember\nREMOVE\nYOUR\nSHOES\nAll Door Exits\nMove away\nfrom slide\nareas\nJUMP\n(DON'T SIT)\nWalk to rear\nof wing\nMove away from\nslide areas\nSTAY ON YOUR FEET\nAND JUMP\nJUMP -\n(DON'T SIT)",
      "SNAP\nOxygen Supply\nC ML ST - ES2005\nPrinted in New Zealand"
    ],
